Subject: [PATCH 0031] rs480: gated-state plain-read DISP2 probe (HAZARD)

Add radeon_rs480_gated_read, the inverse of the force-clock node: it CLEARS a
domain SCLK_CNTL FORCE bit, PLAIN-reads, and restores, to answer whether a
force_clock_validated register is safe to read when the clock is genuinely
gated.  The table holds only inactive-DISP2 CRTC2 registers (the second pipe
drives no display on the Vostro 1000, so clearing FORCE_DISP2 cannot blank the
visible panel).  Disarmed by default (radeon_rs480_gated_read_index == -1).

HAZARD: reset-less K8.  If the plain read stalls while the FORCE bit is clear,
the restore never runs and both cores freeze (physical power cycle).  Attended
use only.

Assisted-by: Claude (Opus 4.8)
